---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import CopyButton from '../components/CopyButton';
import { readmeCode, readmeFamilies } from '../lib/readme';
const asset = (path: string) => `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/${path}`;
const repo = 'https://github.com/huacnlee/nsh-omarchy';
const rustApp = readmeCode('rust');
const tsxApp = readmeCode('tsx');
const install = 'nsh add nsh-omarchy';
const dependency = `[dependencies]
nsh-omarchy = "0.1"`;
const families = readmeFamilies();
const themes = { light: 'github-light', dark: 'tokyo-night' } as const;
---
<Page title="NSH Omarchy — Omarchy components for Native Shell apps" description="Build Native Shell apps in Rust or TSX with Omarchy components that follow the system theme. Try the live gallery, then add one nshm with nsh add.">
  <main id="main" class="shell">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <h1 id="hero-title" class="hero-brand">NSH / OMARCHY</h1>
      <p class="lead">Omarchy components for <a class="text-link" href="https://nsh.dev/">Native Shell</a> apps, in Rust and TSX.<br />Built on <a class="text-link" href="https://nsh.dev/modules/nsh-base/">nsh-base</a>. Guided by <a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/huacnlee/omarchy-style">Omarchy Style</a>.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#start">Get started</a><a class="button" href="#components">Try the components</a></div>
      <p class="hero-note">One nshm · Rust and TSX · MIT licensed</p>
    </section>

    <section id="components" class="live-gallery" aria-label="Live NSH Omarchy gallery">
      <h2 class="sr-only">Try the components</h2>
      <iframe src={asset('gallery/index.html')} title="NSH Omarchy component gallery running in the browser" loading="lazy"></iframe>
      <p class="gallery-caption">The TSX gallery, running in your browser on NSH's web backend: the nsh-omarchy crate in WebAssembly, the app in JavaScript. <a class="text-link" href={asset('gallery/index.html')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open gallery ↗</a> · <a class="text-link" href={`${repo}/tree/main/examples/tsx-gallery`}>View example source</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="catalog-title">
      <div class="section-head"><div><h2 id="catalog-title">Every control a desktop app needs.</h2><p>Each one is a single Rust component: Rust calls its constructor, TSX imports the same component. The <a class="text-link" href={asset('api/')}>API reference</a> lists every prop, shorthand and event.</p></div></div>
      <div class="catalog">
        {families.map(({ family, components }) => (
          <div>
            <h3>{family}</h3>
            <ul class="catalog-items">{components.map((name) => <li>{name}</li>)}</ul>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section split" id="foundation">
      <div><h2>Built on nsh-base.<br />Designed for Omarchy.</h2><p>Omarchy is more than a palette: square corners, one accent, foreground-tinted state fills, a visible focus border and compact desktop type.</p><p>The colors follow the Omarchy theme the system uses and switch live when it changes. Without Omarchy, it draws Tokyo Night or Flexoki Light.</p></div>
      <dl class="principles">
        <div><dt><a href="https://nsh.dev/">Native Shell</a> — the platform</dt><dd>One app in Rust, TSX or both, drawn with each platform's own views on one Rust engine: macOS, Linux, Windows, iOS, Android and the web.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="https://nsh.dev/modules/nsh-base/">nsh-base</a> — the behavior</dt><dd>Focus, keyboard, popups and accessibility, with no look of its own. nsh-omarchy is the presentation on top of it.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="https://github.com/longbridge/nsh/blob/main/website/docs/nshm.md">nshm</a> — one package for both languages</dt><dd>The library is one Rust crate. A Rust app depends on it; a TSX app installs it with <code>nsh add</code> and imports it from <code>"nsh-omarchy"</code>.</dd></div>
        <div><dt><a href="https://github.com/huacnlee/omarchy-style">Omarchy Style</a> — the design language</dt><dd>Square geometry, outlined actions and keyboard-first controls, read from the system's Omarchy palette.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section id="start" class="section">
      <div class="section-head"><div><h2>Add it to your app.</h2><p>In an NSH app's directory, add the nshm. It lists the module in <code>nsh.json</code>, and a Rust app also gets the crate in <code>Cargo.toml</code>.</p></div></div>
      <div class="code-frame install"><div class="code-bar"><span>Terminal</span><CopyButton client:load text={install} /></div><Code code={install} lang="sh" themes={themes} defaultColor="dark" /></div>
      <div class="lang-tabs" data-lang-tabs>
        <div class="lang-tablist" role="tablist" aria-label="App language">
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-tsx" aria-controls="panel-tsx" aria-selected="true">TSX</button>
          <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-rust" aria-controls="panel-rust" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Rust</button>
        </div>
        <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-tsx" aria-labelledby="tab-tsx" class="lang-panel">
          <p>Import the components from <code>"nsh-omarchy"</code>. Props and events are the Rust names in camelCase.</p>
          <div class="code-frame"><div class="code-bar"><span>App.tsx</span><span>TSX</span></div><Code code={tsxApp} lang="tsx" themes={themes} defaultColor="dark" /></div>
        </div>
        <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-rust" aria-labelledby="tab-rust" class="lang-panel" hidden>
          <p><code>nsh add</code> puts the crate in <code>Cargo.toml</code>, or declare it yourself: <code>{dependency.split('\n')[1]}</code>. A constructor takes the required content; the rest are builders.</p>
          <div class="code-frame"><div class="code-bar"><span>src/lib.rs</span><span>Rust</span></div><Code code={rustApp} lang="rust" themes={themes} defaultColor="dark" /></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm mt-6"><a class="text-link" href={asset('api/')}>Read the API reference</a> · <a class="text-link" href={`${repo}#readme`}>Read the README</a> · <a class="text-link" href="https://crates.io/crates/nsh-omarchy">crates.io</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <script>
    // The language tabs of "Add it to your app": TSX first; arrows, Home and End move between them.
    for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-lang-tabs]')) {
      const tabs = [...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[role="tab"]')];
      const select = (tab: HTMLButtonElement, focus = false) => {
        for (const other of tabs) {
          const selected = other === tab;
          other.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(selected));
          other.tabIndex = selected ? 0 : -1;
          document.getElementById(other.getAttribute('aria-controls')!)!.hidden = !selected;
        }
        if (focus) tab.focus();
      };
      for (const tab of tabs) {
        tab.addEventListener('click', () => select(tab));
        tab.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
          const index = tabs.indexOf(tab);
          const next = { ArrowRight: index + 1, ArrowLeft: index - 1, Home: 0, End: tabs.length - 1 }[event.key];
          if (next === undefined) return;
          event.preventDefault();
          select(tabs[(next + tabs.length) % tabs.length], true);
        });
      }
    }
  </script>
</Page>
